        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;padding:4cqw;border-radius:3cqw;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2cqw'><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:2cqw'><div style='min-width:0'><div style='font-size:2.2cqw;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Collection</div><div style='font-weight:600;font-size:4cqw;line-height:1.2;color:#0f172a;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>Ideas</div></div><div style='font-size:2.2cqw;color:#64748b;white-space:nowrap'>17 graphs</div></div><div style='flex:1;min-height:0;overflow:auto'><div style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(26.2cqw,1fr));gap:1.4cqw;align-content:start'><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/active-fragment-authoring-scope/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>A</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Active Fragment Authoring Scope</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Define active fragment focus as an authoring scope, not only a presentation preview.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/bridge-editor/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>The Bridge Editor</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Put everything a Bridge does, including the events it exposes and consumes and the reactions to them, in the Bridge&#39;s own editor.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/edge-and-label-navigation/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>I</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Idea Template</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Modern declaration-first template for framing, testing, and advancing an idea.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/edge-endpoint-reassignment/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>E</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Edge Endpoint Reassignment</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>An interaction model for unplugging one endpoint of an existing edge and reconnecting it to another compatible Port without destroying the relationship.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/event-handler-behavior/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>W</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>What an Event Handler Node Should Do</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A working graph defining an Event Handler as one Event bound directly to one Method.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/mcp-copy-paste-workflow/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>M</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>MCP Without Losing Copy/Paste</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Explore MCP as an optional connected transport for live graph collaboration while preserving copy/paste as Twilite’s universal reviewed workflow.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/method-node-design/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>A</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>A Solid Method Node</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A working graph for designing a Method node as a small, reviewable contract for Event Handlers to call.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/multi-declaration-expansion/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>O</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>One Node, Multiple Declarations</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Define how one semantic node participates in multiple graphs and expands another graph without losing identity.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/node-template-brainstorm/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>W</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>What Could a Node Template Be?</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A brainstorm about a node template, given that a page template and an edge class template already exist: what it would hold, how it relates to them, and what it must not become.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/page-template/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>The Page Template</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A template for a full page view built from named page pieces, so a page is organized as a graph of small parts instead of one large document.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/resource-resolution-and-web-content/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>R</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Resource Resolution and Web Content</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Separate resource authority from representation so Twilite can treat the Web as a native resource space.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/retune-semantic-zoom-thresholds/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>R</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Retune Semantic Zoom Thresholds</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A framed idea about widening the icon zoom band and pushing detail closer to full zoom, prompted by live use of the workspace.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/semantic-zoom-architecture/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>S</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Semantic Zoom Has No Middle Ground</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Four separate mechanisms in Twilite share the name &quot;semantic zoom&quot; and do not share a model. None of them ever repacks a layout: content scales, a node&#39;s own view swaps, and a whole graph collapses to an icon, but a graph&#39;s authored positions never move. A sparsely laid-out graph looks the same fraction empty at every zoom, right up until it vanishes into one icon.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/stroke-control/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>The Stroke Control</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Make the stroke widget a small graph of its own, with real Properties, a self-updating preview and a Bridge, so an edge class is edited through composed controls.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/twilite-front-door/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Twilite Front Door</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Make the first ninety seconds of Twilite explain the product by letting the visitor navigate it.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/typed-inter-graph-handoff-envelope/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Typed Inter-Graph Handoff Envelope</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Specify the inspectable typed envelope that carries values between declared graph ports without coupling connectivity, expansion, and execution.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/zoom-and-wheel-behavior/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>The Camera Behaves Like the Browser</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>A gesture contract for zoom and the mouse wheel in Twilite: browser zoom drives the camera, and the wheel acts on the surface under the pointer the way it does on the web, panning the camera when that surface has nothing to scroll.</span></span></a></div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
